🗂️ Flashcards (self-test)
Q: Difference between <> and !=? A: None — both mean "not equal". <> is the ANSI standard.

Q: Is BETWEEN 100 AND 500 inclusive? A: Yes — includes both 100 and 500.

Q: Which is faster to write: 3 chained ORs or IN? A: IN — same result, cleaner and easier to maintain.

Q: What does % match in LIKE? A: Any number of characters (zero, one, or many). _ matches exactly one.

Q: Pattern for a name ending with "n"? A: LIKE '%n'

Q: Pattern for 3rd letter = "r"? A: LIKE '__r%' (two underscores, then r, then anything)

Q: When mixing AND and OR, what must you use? A: Parentheses () — AND binds tighter than OR.

Q: NOT score < 500 is the same as...? A: score >= 500

✅ Practice Checklist
